/**
@fn FLAG_NO_STEAL
# Use
<table>
	<tr>
		<th>Type(s)</th>
		<th>Description</th>
	</tr>	<tr>
		<td>
@ref page_type_72
		</td><td>            An item with &lt;cannot be stolen&gt; cannot be taken out of a
            creature's inventory with the stealing skill. Flesh items generated
            from a creature's &lt;treasurelist&gt; get this flag set
            automatically, together with their name, level and resistances, so
            you only need to set it by hand on items you place into an
            inventory yourself.

            The flag is cleared again whenever the object is inserted into a
            map. Setting it on an item lying on the floor therefore has no
            effect: an item keeps it only for as long as it stays in an
            inventory.</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td>
@ref page_type_215, @ref page_type_28
		</td><td>                A creature with &lt;guards inventory&gt; has already noticed a
                thief and lets nothing more be taken from it. While it can
                detect the thief it calls for help, loses &lt;unaggressive&gt;
                and the steal attempt fails outright. If it cannot detect the
                thief it raises its own &lt;wisdom&gt; instead, making it harder
                to steal from next time.

                The server sets this flag by itself as soon as a steal attempt
                is noticed, so you only need to set it here to make a creature
                suspicious from the very start.

                The singing skill shares this flag: a creature with &lt;guards
                inventory&gt; cannot be calmed by singing, and a creature that
                has been sung to cannot be stolen from afterwards. Unlike on
                items, this flag is not cleared when the creature is inserted
                into a map.</td>
	</tr>

*/
